        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Waputik Mountains\n- People: George M. Dawson\n- Animals: mountain goat, Oreamnos americanus\n- Languages and Ethnic Groups: Stoney Indian\n- Topics: place names, etymology\n\nFacts:\n- In 1884, George M. Dawson named the Waputik Mountains.\n- The name \"waputik\" is the Stoney Indian word for \"white goat.\"\n- The mountain goat is also known as the Rocky Mountain goat.\n- The mountain goat has the scientific name Oreamnos americanus.\n- The mountain goat is a large hoofed mammal endemic to North America.",
